Track 3: The Roof-Deck Prism Spectator
- Story & Context: On the final night of the Old Town Film Festival, the group snuck a two-ton glass projection prism onto the slate roof of the abandoned Odeon cinema to capture the morning light through their telescope lenses. When the sunrise hit the glass, it cast a blinding rainbow spectrum across the crowd just as the bagpipes hit an impossible, nine-second euphoric note over a churning, sub-heavy jungle chop. The dawn security guards dropped their flashlights and began to dance, cementing the legendary morning as the moment the underground film ravers permanently claimed the sky. "We turned the silver beam into our own sun!" became the shouted chant that echoed down the alleyways long after the sound system was packed away.
